# The fallback mirror for the mesa release tarball. Read by ./fetch-source.sh, which is the one
# fetch shared by all three mesa builds (packages/mesa via makepkg, packages/mesa-x86,
# packages/mesa-android).
#
# WHY A SEPARATE FILE, and not a field in ./source.pin: packages/inputhash.sh hashes source.pin
# into rootfs/manifest.lock's `novadeck` rows, so anything in there is a claim that changing it
# changes what gets BUILT. A mirror location cannot change that -- fetch-source.sh verifies the
# tarball against the sha256 pinned in ./PKGBUILD no matter which host answered, and refuses
# anything else. Keeping the value here means refreshing it costs neither a `make relock` nor a
# full mesa rebuild for a byte-identical artifact.
#
# WHY FEDORA'S LOOKASIDE. It serves the PRISTINE upstream tarball, byte-identical -- confirmed for
# 26.2.1 by fetching it and comparing against our pinned sha256. It is independently hosted from
# freedesktop, which is the entire point: archive.mesa3d.org is one machine
# (annarchy.freedesktop.org) with no CDN, and mesa.freedesktop.org is Fastly-fronted but fills
# from that same origin, so the two fail together. MEASURED 2026-08-23: both unreachable for over
# half an hour. The alternatives were checked and rejected -- Debian repacks mesa, Gentoo's
# distfiles did not carry 26.2.1, and sources.archlinux.org does not rehost it.
#
#   sha512  SHA512 of the tarball, used ONLY to build the mirror's URL: Fedora's lookaside embeds
#           it in the path. NOT an integrity check -- the sha256 in ./PKGBUILD is, and it is the
#           hash that was verified against upstream's PGP signature.
#
# ON A MESA BUMP: read the new value from the directory index at
#
#   https://src.fedoraproject.org/repo/pkgs/mesa/mesa-<ver>.tar.xz/sha512/
#
# If Fedora has not packaged the version yet, leave the field EMPTY (`sha512:` with nothing after
# it). fetch-source.sh then behaves exactly as the builds did before a mirror existed -- upstream
# or a clear failure -- rather than pretending to have a fallback. Getting the value WRONG costs a
# 404 on the fallback path only; it can never produce a wrong build.
sha512: 42e793561661a567e72c7324d071ab9f82d3a9f1e000827ed989b8d5fcc2cd16e50c02808d43465b3135c25a3cad77649ba0bf9e35d95b848f8fc8d8b9ce327c
